tted_at":"2026-08-17T17:32:16Z"},{"id":4953466668,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJz_nLA","state":"APPROVED","commit_id":"e1b982976740085cb118e844158a9df8e4283ba4","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","login":"dsnopek","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek"},"body":"I tested this with WebXR on both the Immersive Web Emulator and a Meta Quest Pro in Meta's browser - it seemed to work fine!\r\n\r\n~~If Emscripten has added their own implementation of `glFramebufferTextureMultiviewOVR()`, we may also be able to remove ours in `library_godot_webgl.js` and `godot_webgl2.h` (not just the type info in `library_godot_webgl2.extern.js` for Closure), but that's something we can try in a follow-up~~\r\n\r\n**UPDATE:** I dug a bit into the Emscripten source code for version 6.0.1, and it doesn't look like they have an implementation for `glFramebufferTextureMultiviewOVR()`. If I had to guess, I think this Emscripten update came with a Closure update, and it's Closure that added type info for it, but there's still no implementation","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122412#pullrequestreview-4953466668","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122412","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2026-08-17T18:32:45Z"},{"id":4960387215,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJ6mAjw","state":"APPROVED","commit_id":"e1b982976740085cb118e844158a9df8e4283ba4","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?u=af70f5d107e9c1447f296643d5a566dab53d25e8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z",